# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We are committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and inclusive environment for everyone participating in this project. We welcome contributions from people of all backgrounds and experience levels.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

- Being respectful and considerate.
- Using welcoming and inclusive language.
- Accepting constructive criticism.
- Focusing on what is best for the project and community.
- Showing empathy toward other contributors.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, discrimination, personal attacks, offensive comments, and other conduct that creates an unsafe or unwelcoming environment.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of this Code of Conduct. They may take appropriate and fair corrective action when unacceptable behavior occurs.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces, including the GitHub repository, issues, pull requests, discussions, and other project-related interactions.

## Enforcement

Instances of unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers. Maintainers will review reports and take appropriate action based on the circumstances.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers will respond to reported incidents fairly and consistently. Possible actions may include a warning, removal of inappropriate content, temporary restriction of participation, or permanent removal from project activities.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is inspired by community standards and the Contributor Covenant. It has been adapted for this project.
